# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD runs entrypoint.ps1, which starts sshd + WinRM, launches
# GlassFish domain1 as a DETACHED child process, then execs an idle loop as PID 1.
# So:
#   * the GlassFish admin (:4848) and app (:8080) listeners are ALREADY UP when the
#     agent starts — verify.ps1's live traversal + 8080 checks have something to hit,
#     and the "fixed the keyfile but never restarted the domain" case stays detectable;
#   * PID 1 is the idle loop, so the solution's restart-domain cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must talk to / RESTART the running domain, not
# assume it needs cold-starting — the vulnerable domain is already serving.
